IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Schedule 4 Dictionary: the table of defined terms.
--
-- Section 3(3): "The Dictionary in Schedule 4 defines certain terms used in Acts and instruments."
-- Each entry below keeps the term as printed, the connective the text uses (means, includes, ...),
-- the words of the definition and, in members, the paragraphs and any closing words as printed.
-- The Dictionary is a list that does not say it is closed, so a term that is not in it is not covered (NOTHING).
-- Generated from the text file by a script (see NOTES.md); the structured definitions are in nsw-definitions.l4.

DECLARE DefinitionKind IS ONE OF
    Means
    Includes
    MeansAndIncludes
    HasTheSameMeaningAs
    HasTheMeaningProvidedFor
    IsDefinedIn
    SeeReference
    MeaningGivenByParagraphs

DECLARE DictionaryEntry HAS
    term IS A STRING
    names IS A LIST OF STRING
    kind IS A DefinitionKind
    words IS A STRING
    members IS A LIST OF STRING

-- src:940 | affidavit, in the case of persons for the time being allowed by law to affirm, declare or promise, includes affirmation, declaration and promise.
